---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';
import PageShell from '../../components/PageShell.astro';
---

<Layout 
    title="Editorial Policy & Reference Standards | Real BMI"
    description="Read our editorial policy for evidence-based health content, peer-reviewed methodology, clinical screening definitions, and transparent user guidance."
    canonicalURL="https://realbmicalculator.com/en/editorial-policy/"
>
    <Navbar />
    <PageShell
      title="Editorial Policy"
      eyebrow="Methodology & Transparency"
      description="How Bhawanshi Dosi researches, references, and maintains evidence-based health tools and educational content."
      returnUrl="/en/"
      returnLabel="Home"
    >
      <div class="max-w-5xl space-y-8 prose prose-zinc dark:prose-invert text-[var(--muted-foreground)] leading-relaxed text-base sm:text-lg font-medium opacity-90">
        <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-normal text-[var(--foreground)] leading-relaxed">
          Welcome to <strong>Real BMI</strong>, an independent digital health calculation and educational platform created and maintained by <strong>Bhawanshi Dosi</strong> in Banswara, Rajasthan, India. Our mission is to provide transparent, scientifically grounded calculation tools that help individuals, students, educators, and community health workers evaluate basic biometric indicators—such as Body Mass Index (BMI), Basal Metabolic Rate (BMR), and Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE)—freely and privately.
        </p>

        <!-- 1. Evidence-Based Guidelines & Standards -->
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            1. Evidence-Based Guidelines & Standards
          </h2>
          <p>
            All computational algorithms and reference ranges on Real BMI are derived directly from published medical literature and authoritative public health guidelines:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5 text-sm sm:text-base">
            <li><strong>World Health Organization (WHO):</strong> International adult BMI classifications (TRS 854), Western Pacific regional Asian action thresholds (23.0 kg/m² overweight, 27.5 kg/m² obesity), and waist-to-hip ratio cutoffs.</li>
            <li><strong>Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC):</strong> Population reference metrics, pediatric growth percentile reference standards, and adult screening frameworks.</li>
            <li><strong>Indian Council of Medical Research (ICMR):</strong> Specific consensus thresholds for Asian Indians accounting for the South Asian 'thin-fat' phenotype (increased visceral adiposity at lower BMI).</li>
            <li><strong>Peer-Reviewed Research:</strong> Landmark mathematical formulations published by researchers, including Mifflin-St Jeor (resting energy expenditure), Devine (ideal body weight), Mosteller (body surface area), Boer (lean body mass), and Hodgdon (U.S. Navy circumference regression).</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 2. Author Identity & Standards -->
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            2. Author Identity & Standards
          </h2>
          <p>
            Real BMI operates under an open, individual developer model with full personal accountability:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5 text-sm sm:text-base">
            <li><strong>Founder & Software Engineer:</strong> <strong>Bhawanshi Dosi</strong> is the sole developer and author responsible for all software engineering, formula coding, automated unit testing, and design architecture.</li>
            <li><strong>Client-Side Zero-Retention Privacy:</strong> All calculations execute 100% locally in your web browser using JavaScript. Biological measurements (height, weight, age, waist) never leave your device and are never saved to databases or remote servers.</li>
            <li><strong>Non-Clinical Educational Resource:</strong> Real BMI is an independent informational website. It is not an accredited hospital, clinical medical practice, or formal medical review board. All calculators provide educational screening estimates and do not constitute clinical evaluations.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 3. Transparency & Continuous Updates -->
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            3. Transparency & Continuous Updates
          </h2>
          <p>
            We believe that algorithmic health tools must be fully open and auditable. Every calculator page displays the exact mathematical formula, unit conversion logic, input requirements, physiological limitations, and direct links to indexed landmark studies (PubMed / DOI). We do not employ black-box estimation algorithms.
          </p>
          <p>
            To ensure global accessibility, all 23 computational health tools are maintained across six languages (English, Spanish, French, German, Korean, and Hindi) with consistent mathematical logic.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 4. Editorial Independence & Advertising Ethics -->
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            4. Editorial Independence & Advertising Ethics
          </h2>
          <p>
            To keep all health tools freely accessible without subscription paywalls, Real BMI is funded through privacy-friendly digital advertisements served via Google AdSense.
          </p>
          <p>
            We enforce a strict editorial firewall: advertisers, sponsors, and pharmaceutical manufacturers have zero influence over our algorithms, clinical caveats, or written articles. We never accept sponsored calculation results, paid search rankings, or commercial product placements.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 5. Educational Disclaimer & Clinical Boundaries -->
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            5. Educational Disclaimer & Clinical Boundaries
          </h2>
          <p>
            All calculations and guides on Real BMI are educational proxies designed for general health awareness and personal screening. They are not medical diagnostic instruments, treatment protocols, or individualized dietary plans.
          </p>
          <p>
            Anthropometric indices cannot evaluate individual factors such as lean muscle mass, bone density, hydration, or medical history. Users should always consult a licensed physician, registered dietitian, or qualified healthcare provider before initiating weight loss programs or making clinical decisions.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 6. Review Cycle & Automated Testing -->
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            6. Review Cycle & Automated Testing
          </h2>
          <p>
            We follow a structured bi-annual review protocol for all formulas, reference tables, and clinical boundaries. When authoritative health organizations (WHO, CDC, ICMR) issue revised consensus statements, our calculation models are systematically cross-referenced against the updated primary literature.
          </p>
          <p>
            Software quality is maintained through comprehensive automated test suites. Over 500 unit tests verify mathematical parity between metric and imperial units (with a strict 0.01 tolerance) and validate edge-case inputs prior to every production release.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 7. Human Authorship & Originality -->
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            7. Human Authorship & Originality
          </h2>
          <p>
            All written guides, worked calculation examples, FAQs, and methodology documents are authored originally by Bhawanshi Dosi with direct cross-referencing to primary scientific papers.
          </p>
          <p>
            We do not publish unverified, scraped, or automated AI-generated health content. Every paragraph undergoes manual review for scientific accuracy, tone clarity, and strict adherence to evidence-based medical consensus.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 8. Corrections Policy & Feedback Protocol -->
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            8. Corrections Policy & Feedback Protocol
          </h2>
          <p>
            Scientific accuracy is our foremost standard. If you identify a mathematical discrepancy, an ambiguous definition, or an outdated citation, we encourage you to report it directly through our <a href="/en/contact/" class="text-[var(--accent)] underline font-medium">Contact & Support Page</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Verified corrections are investigated promptly, implemented in our live codebase within 24 to 48 hours, and transparently documented in our project version history.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 9. Pre-Publication Review & Privacy Protocol -->
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            9. Pre-Publication Review & Privacy Protocol
          </h2>
          <p>
            Before any new tool or article goes live, it completes a 4-step quality assurance verification:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5 text-sm sm:text-base">
            <li><strong>Step 1: Literature Verification:</strong> Equations and cutoff tables are verified against primary peer-reviewed journals and official WHO/CDC monographs.</li>
            <li><strong>Step 2: Mathematical Parity Testing:</strong> Dual-unit regression tests confirm identical mathematical behavior across metric (kg, cm) and imperial (lbs, inches) systems.</li>
            <li><strong>Step 3: Privacy & Security Audit:</strong> Mandatory verification confirms that no personal data or session identifiers are transmitted, logged, or stored.</li>
            <li><strong>Step 4: Editorial & Clarity Review:</strong> Formatting, citations, contextual disclosures, and readability are verified prior to public deployment.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </div>
    </PageShell>
</Layout>
